  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">E-Governance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Kosovo):  .The E-Governance Activity will continue to provide technical assistance and training to the Government of Kosovo to enhance digital service delivery to citizens, strengthen transparency and oversight mechanisms, improve management of digital security and systems, and engage civil society and the private sector in digital development. With FY24 funds, the Activity will support implementation of Kosovo&apos;s e-Government Strategy, including reforms for the Agency for Information Society (AIS) and the establishment of the Data Management Unit (DMU). The Activity will strengthen the coordination and planning of digital public services among key institutions and provide these institutions with technical expertise to ensure secure, quality digital platforms and effective service delivery. The activity will enable institutions to work together, sharing diverse perspectives, to identify and prioritize e-services that are most needed and establish transparency, oversight and feedback mechanisms within the eKosova platform to optimize digital service delivery through the engagement of civil society organizations and the private sector. The Activity aligns with CAATSA Goal 1 supporting Cybersecurity (10% of funding) and CAATSA Goal 2 promoting rule of law (30% of funding).  The Activity also contributes to ICS Objective 1.3 and 2.2 by supporting a fully functional governmental e-portal to enhance citizen services, a key area supporting Kosovo&apos;s readiness for EU accession. This activity contributes to the democracy directive and the critical issues of: Anti-Corruption, Gender Equality/Women&apos;s Empowerment-Secondary, and Digital Technology...</narrative>
  </description>
